  "articleBody": "Planning a kitchen addition expands your living space, but committing to a contractor requires close evaluation before signing a contract. Expanding your home involves structural changes, tying into the existing roof and foundation, and extending electrical and plumbing lines.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\n\n- Does the written scope detail allowance structures, change orders, and payment terms clearly?\n- Who handles local permits and code reviews for zoning, structural, and fire requirements?\n- How are specialized sub-trades coordinated for plumbing and electrical work?\n- What is the contractor’s hands-on experience with additions of a similar square footage?\n\nA reliable general contractor provides a clear path forward, keeping communication direct and transparent. Municipal regulations generally require engineered project plans reviewed against local zoning and safety codes before groundbreaking. When you alter exterior walls or foundation lines, having a single accountable point of contact ensures framing, insulation, and finish carpentry align smoothly.\n\nIf you are planning an addition in Aurora or the Denver metro area, talk to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC. As an owner-operated team with an A+ BBB rating, we handle custom framing, drywall, and finish carpentry while coordinating all mechanical trades. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your kitchen plans.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
